<title>USA: Cordiant's Bates wins global Clorets account.</title>
<headline>Cordiant's Bates wins global Clorets account.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cordiant Plc's Bates Worldwide said it has won Warner-Lambert Co's Clorets brand advertising, which had been handled by its rival, WPP Group Plc's J. Walter Thompson.</p>
<p>The advertising is worth an estimated $15 million to $20 million in annual billings.</p>
<p>Bates already handles a number of Warner-Lambert products, including Dentyne, Certs, Actifed, Sudafed and Sinutab.</p>
</text>
